%T A401499 740,816,896,980,1068,1156,1244,1336,1432,1532,1636,1740,1844,1952,
%U A401499 2064,2180,2296,2412,2528,2648,2772,2900,3028,3156,3292,3436,3584,3736,3888,4044,4200
%N A401499 Place n points at the integer polar angles of the Archimedean spiral r = k, 0 <= k < n, then around the k-th point draw a circle whose radius is the distance from the k-th point to the (k+1)-th point: a(n) is the number of (curved) edges in the resulting planar graph.
%C A401499 See A401497 for further details.
%H A401499 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A401499/b401499.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A401499 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A401499/a401499.jpg">Image for n = 5</a>. The center of the circles are shown as white dots.
%H A401499 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archimedean_spiral">Archimedean spiral</a>.
%F A401499 a(n) = A401497(n) + A401498(n) - 1, n > 1, by Euler's formula.
%F A401499 a(n) = 2*n*(n - 1) for 1 <= n <= 15.
%Y A401499 Cf. A401497 (regions), A401498 (vertices), A371375, A385162, A374339.
%K A401499 nonn,new
%O A401499 1,2
%A A401499 _Scott R. Shannon_, Oct 27 2026
